 This gem depends on some private git repositories and it is not meant to be used by third parties. But we hope it can serve as inspiration for anyone wanting to run fizzy on their own infrastructure.
 
+
+### Localizing Fizzy
+
+Add application copy to both `config/locales/en.yml` and `ja.yml`. Translate whole messages, using named interpolations for values, and `_html` translations for messages containing markup. Keep user content and identifiers (such as event names, form values and DOM IDs) separate from their labels. Use `l` for displayed dates; keep wire formats such as URL dates and JSON timestamps locale-independent.
+
+Stimulus controllers can import `t` from `helpers/i18n` for messages in the `client` scope. Mailers use `localized_mail` so the subject and all parts are rendered for the recipient rather than the sender or job worker.
+
+Mission Control supplies English-only views and normally forces an English locale. Its Japanese Rails view overrides under `app/views/{layouts/,}mission_control` are based on the MIT-licensed `mission_control-jobs` 1.1.0 templates. Check them when upgrading that dependency. The rich-text editor package uses its own strings.
